Run away, run away!!

I really like pets, myself.  What I'd do in that situation is try to
engrave Elbereth enough to get the ant(s) away and run for the stairs. 
Alternately, blind them and run (but not both).  Then come back later. 
Soldier ants are *very* dangerous.  Also, you could engrave elbereth (even
w/ fingers) and then toss darts as the ants run away.  +2 darts rock :)

The mines are where pets really shine (and really eat lots of corpses :-p)
If they can take out a guard, you're doing *very* well - you can get a
whistle, which helps keep them near you (it's still a pain).  If they are
close by when you use it, they'll come towards you.  And minetown (and/or
the mines in general) often has a magic whistle...

Try playing a pacifist healer a few times.  You'll die miserable deaths
really often, and it'll really suck, but you'll learn a *lot* from it, and
the next time you try a more reasonable character, it'll be so nice to be
able to smack down the occational monster that gets past your pet!

To be honest, I think of pets as a first line of defense - they thin the
field for me.  I don't expect them to take out super-badass monsters. 
WHen those come up, I run away/cower/fight (or switch from one to the
other as need be :) )  Remember missle weapons are you friend!

